{
    "metadata": {
        "description": "Cross-publisher trip planner that composes flight_finder and hotel_finder from independent origins, with one client-side computation tool.",
        "tags": ["agent_web", "demo", "trip_planner"],
        "sample_queries": [
            "SFO to Tokyo around June 14-21, hotel near Shinjuku under $300/night with a gym. My email is bob@example.com.",
        ],
        "branding": {
            "name": "TravelGenius",
            "tagline": "One question, every itinerary",
            "logo": "✨",
            "primary_color": "#6D28D9",
            "accent_color": "#0EA5A4",
            "background": "#FAF7FF",
            "foreground": "#1f1a2e",
            "muted": "#6e6587",
            "card": "#ffffff",
            "font_stack": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Inter', sans-serif",
        },
    },
    "llm_config": {
        "model_name": "claude-haiku",
        # BYOK: trip_planner is the user-facing top-level agent in this demo,
        # so its LLM call uses the client's own Anthropic key. The key is
        # supplied in sly_data.llm_config.anthropic_api_key on each request.
        # The provider-specific field name matters: ChatAnthropic reads
        # `anthropic_api_key`, not `api_key`. See
        # neuro_san.internals.run_context.langchain.llms.anthropic_llm_policy.
        "anthropic_api_key": "sly_data",
    },
    "tools": [
        {
            "name": "trip_planner",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Plans a trip end-to-end by composing flight options from flights.example
with hotel options from hotels.example, then summing the total cost using
a client-side tool.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "request": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The full trip request in plain English"
                        },
                    },
                    "required": ["request"]
                },
            },
            "instructions": """
You are a cross-publisher trip planner.

When the user describes a trip, do the following:

1. Call the flight_finder external agent with the relevant details
   (origin, destination, dates).  Capture the flight options it returns
   and remember a chosen recommended option.
2. Call the hotel_finder external agent with the relevant details
   (city, checkin, checkout, max price, requested amenities).  Capture
   the top-ranked hotel.
3. Call total_cost with the recommended flight price and hotel nightly
   price * number of nights.
4. Reply to the user with a concise itinerary recommendation that
   includes the flight_id, the hotel name, and the total estimated cost
   in USD.

If, on a follow-up message, the user asks to "hold" or "book" a flight
option, call the flight_finder external agent again and pass through the
hold request along with sly_data.passenger_email.
""",
            "tools": [
                "http://localhost:8801/flight_finder",
                "http://localhost:8802/hotel_finder",
                "total_cost",
            ],
            "allow": {
                "to_downstream": {
                    "sly_data": {
                        # Forward the user's BYOK LLM credentials into every
                        # downstream agent so each origin's LLM call bills
                        # the same client, not the origin operator. Trust
                        # implication: every origin in the chain sees the
                        # client's key; only invoke chains you trust.
                        "llm_config": true,
                        "passenger_email": true,
                    },
                },
                "from_downstream": {
                    "sly_data": ["last_booking_code"],
                },
                "to_upstream": {
                    "sly_data": ["last_booking_code"],
                },
            },
        },

        {
            "name": "total_cost",
            "function": {
                "description": "Sums flight cost and hotel nightly cost * nights to give a total trip USD cost",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "flight_cost_usd": {"type": "number"},
                        "hotel_nightly_usd": {"type": "number"},
                        "nights": {"type": "integer"},
                    },
                    "required": ["flight_cost_usd", "hotel_nightly_usd", "nights"],
                },
            },
            "client_side": true,
            "class": "total_cost.TotalCost",
        },
    ],
}
